From 6157b6af16d84b7c7fb31642965a7bafb5024116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Goose contributors <goose@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:24:35 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Describe the native interface as JSON

Expose compiler-resolved exports and reachable layouts for language-neutral
binding generation and ABI verification through --emit-interface.
---
 docs/goose_spec.md     |   9 ++
 src/capabilities.h     |   2 +-
 src/interface.h        | 211 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/main.cpp           |  22 ++++-
 test/interface_json.py |  54 +++++++++++
 test/run_tests.py      |  27 ++++++
 6 files changed, 322 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/interface.h
 create mode 100644 test/interface_json.py

diff --git a/docs/goose_spec.md b/docs/goose_spec.md
index a85ae506..c3ee3240 100644
--- a/docs/goose_spec.md
+++ b/docs/goose_spec.md
@@ -3279,6 +3279,15 @@ thread. `--header` requires generated C output and at least one export, and
 writes declarations and the required packed C type definitions for the
 exported API.
 
+`--emit-interface out.json` (or `json` for stdout; with `goose check`, it
+writes nothing else) describes the program's C interface for a binding
+generator in another language: each export's name, symbol, documentation,
+parameters and results, each with its Goose type as text and structurally
+(`prim`, `struct`, `enum`, `array`, `slice`, `ref`, `builder`), and every
+struct and enum the exports reach, with each field's offset and size and
+each pad as the C backend lays them out (C.2), and the source files the
+program was compiled from.
+
 An exported C symbol is emitted as written, as an `extern` one is, and must be a
 C identifier that is not a C keyword and that the program does not otherwise
 reserve (`main`, `goose_init`, or a name beginning with `gs_`).
